e problem with this  is it adds nothing and actually it's  it's a really weird addition but again  kind of exemplifies what I was talking  about with  I'm not sure this was a good idea to  adapt in the first place or at least to  try and force into a feature length  running time because this crammed in  added stuff this 25 or however long it  is minutes stuck at the front it's  personal completely detachable all this  extra stuff with Barbara with Batgirl it  it doesn't tie in directly doesn't fit  the matically it is very obviously  padding and it makes for a really  jarring gearshift if you don't already  know the story in some way this your  first time seeing it it's gonna start  out here thinking oh I didn't realize  the Killing Joke was a Batgirl story and  then it and then the Joker finally shows  up a half-hour in and Batgirl basically  just gets her seen him getting shot one  scene in the hospital after that no I  well that was so weird they made it like  it was a Batgirl story but it isn't  exactly and I know why they did it  beyond besides the obvious padding for  runtime thing they were trying to fix  what is generally considered to be the  one problem would be Killing Joke  because the caring joke is a seminal  story and it is incredibly hydrating  highly regarded it's generally regarded  as one of the definitive Batman Joker  stories but if there is a weakness in it  it has to do with Batgirl now I  personally will argue that looking at  the story in isolation she has a very  specific function and it is admittedly  not as a character she her function is  to have what happens to her be traumatic  towards Gordon that is the Joker's only  interest in her and since the story so  Joker centric that's the only use the  story has for her now where that becomes  the problem is in the larger context of  the DC Universe and certainly fans of  Batgirl  hate this story and they hate it because  the character that they love gets  reduced to just being a victim and  that's completely legitimate in that  context but the thing is again if you  read The Killing Joke in isolation  without a ton of background knowledge  about Barbara Gordon as Batgirl then it  just it just becomes a well it's a  functional plot thing  I know that because that's how I  experienced The Killing Joke initially I  read that long before I got in the  background now at this point I love  Batgirl so I get why Batgirl fans really  hate this story but it's only with that  added context that it has that wait but  they went and added that context to this  movie when the story works best without  that extra context of what you actually  lose by crippling Barbara Gordon so by  giving her the extra time and padding it  out and giving us more Batgirl they kind  of make the problem worse they're  actually highlighting how reduced this  character is going from a costumed hero  to a victim and actually I think the  fact that they even thought they should  try and do that  really points to maybe this wasn't a  good idea to adapt in the first place  because honestly if you're gonna try and  fix the Batgirl problem in The Killing  Joke it doesn't really work because the  this story is so tight and is  constructed so specifically that you  can't remove that and obviously they  know that they didn't remove it it's  still in there but trying to fix it  that's like trying to fix the fascist  overtones in the Dark Knight Returns or  trying to fix the capitalistic praising  and atlas shrugs like this is just  something that comes with the territory  and if you're not okay with that  you maybe should just be adapting  something else  look I've been hiding obviously I've  been kind of complaining I've been  picking apart ultimately I feel like it  doesn't justify its own existence that  it brings nothing to the table that the  comic book didn't already do and do  better if I'm honest there's nothing  that this animated version does better  and the new things that spring to the  