o the conclusion that Allen  more stuff is too tailored to what comic  books do well that when you try and  adapt into another medium it's it just  doesn't work as well it doesn't become  flat-out bad because like the ideas are  still good enough that you know you go  oh that's interesting but they're not  communicated nearly as well in fill  as they are in the comic book page so I  guess that's kind of it you know I'm  annoyed with myself because I did  something I almost never do I did a  blind buy on this I actually now own a  copy of it I don't know if I'm ever  gonna want to watch it again I think if  I want my Killing Joke fix I'm gonna  read the book again and now I can  imagine Mark Hamill's delivery as I read  The Joker's lines and pop and honestly  I'll probably get more satisfaction out  of that than actually watching this  thing again so that's my feelings on  Batman The Killing Joke have you seen it  what were your thoughts on it whatever  they were drop something down in the  comments and let's talk about it don't  forget to like subscribe follow me on  twitter at council geek check out the  counselor deeps podcast on itunes and  stitcher and as for me I'll be back as  soon as I can get my next fix

